<title>USA: Regal-Beloit names Kaplan CFO.</title>
<headline>Regal-Beloit names Kaplan CFO.</headline>
<dateline>BELOIT, Wis. 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Regal-Beloit Corp said Thursday Kenneth Kaplan will become chief financial officer in late October, replacing Robert Burress, who is retiring.</p>
<p>Kaplan had been chief financial officer of Gehl Co .</p>
<p>Burress will remain secretary through April, 1997.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
